WEBVTT

00:00:01.283 --> 00:00:02.908
[PHOENIX]
My name is Phoenix Wright.

00:00:02.991 --> 00:00:05.366
And I'm a defense attorney.

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.325
I've been building my
reputation over several cases,

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:11.200
and I'm really starting to
make a name for myself.

00:00:11.283 --> 00:00:13.158
No matter how tough
the case may be,

00:00:13.241 --> 00:00:15.866
or how high the odds are
stacked against us,

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.533
it's my job to
stand up for those

00:00:17.616 --> 00:00:19.491
who have no one else
in their corner.

00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:27.241
[PHOENIX] I'll do whatever it
takes to fight for the truth!

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.408
I suppose I should
take one last look

00:00:32.491 --> 00:00:34.450
at this file before
we get started.

00:00:36.575 --> 00:00:39.450
--[PHOENIX] Hmm...
--[cell jingle plays]

00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:40.950
Hello?

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:44.241
Guess they hung up.

00:00:45.908 --> 00:00:46.950
--[blow lands]
--[PHOENIX grunts]

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.658
[laughter]

00:00:52.741 --> 00:00:55.575
Try not to take this
personally, Mr. Attorney.

00:02:26.116 --> 00:02:28.783
--[cell jingle plays]
--[PHOENIX grunts]

00:02:28.866 --> 00:02:30.533
What the heck is going on?

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.158
[JUDGE]
There is no escape!

00:02:32.241 --> 00:02:34.158
You can run but you
cannot hide from

00:02:34.241 --> 00:02:36.283
the mighty hammer of justice!

00:02:43.366 --> 00:02:46.033
[PHOENIX groans]
Ow...

00:02:50.325 --> 00:02:51.783
[PHOENIX]
Huh...?

00:02:51.866 --> 00:02:54.366
Good morning, Mr. Wright.
Thanks for your help!

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.908
Uh. Sure. And who are you?

00:02:56.991 --> 00:02:59.241
Sir, my name is Maggey Byrde!

00:02:59.325 --> 00:03:02.033
And today I'll be putting my
life into your capable hands!

00:03:02.116 --> 00:03:03.825
Oh. Your life, eh?

00:03:03.908 --> 00:03:05.741
Don't you remember
the promise you made?

00:03:05.825 --> 00:03:08.075
You swore that you could
prove my innocence!

00:03:08.158 --> 00:03:09.408
Did I?

00:03:09.491 --> 00:03:10.741
Yes, and even though all
my friends like to call me

00:03:10.825 --> 00:03:12.200
the "Goddess of Misfortune,"

00:03:12.283 --> 00:03:13.783
what I'm dealing
with now is a tragedy

00:03:13.866 --> 00:03:16.366
on an unbelievably epic scale!

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.241
But when you said you'd
help me, I felt my soul rising

00:03:18.325 --> 00:03:20.825
from the ashes like
a Phoenix, Mr. Wright!

00:03:20.908 --> 00:03:21.950
And that's me?

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:23.950
Right! Phoenix Wright!

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:26.408
I see now. What a crazy name.

00:03:26.491 --> 00:03:29.366
You do believe me?
I promise I didn't kill him!

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:32.658
Whoa! There was a murder?
No! That's horrible!

00:03:32.741 --> 00:03:33.866
--[door opens
--[BOTH] Hmm?

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:36.033
If you're ready,
the trial's about to begin.

00:03:36.116 --> 00:03:37.658
I put my faith in you!

00:03:37.741 --> 00:03:39.325
[PHOENIX chuckles]

00:03:39.408 --> 00:03:40.950
[PHOENIX]
Courtroom Two.

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:03.575
[PHOENIX]
No pressure at all.

00:04:08.616 --> 00:04:11.033
[JUDGE] This court is hereby
in session for the trial

00:04:11.116 --> 00:04:13.200
of Ms. Maggey Byrde!

00:04:13.283 --> 00:04:14.991
[PHOENIX]
Is that old geezer the judge?

00:04:15.075 --> 00:04:16.325
[PAYNE chuckles]

00:04:16.408 --> 00:04:18.908
I knew we'd meet again
someday, Wright.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.116
Right.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.241
[PHOENIX]
This is gonna be a pain.

00:04:22.325 --> 00:04:23.450
[MAGGEY grunts]

00:04:23.533 --> 00:04:25.325
Prosecutor Payne,
are you ready to begin

00:04:25.408 --> 00:04:26.741
your opening statement?

00:04:26.825 --> 00:04:28.991
Quite! Your Honor, today,
I will prove the defendant

00:04:29.075 --> 00:04:30.783
murdered her lover.

00:04:30.866 --> 00:04:32.866
[PHOENIX gasps]
You murdered your lover?

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:35.033
[MAGGEY]
No, it wasn't like that!

00:04:35.116 --> 00:04:37.533
Constable Prince was more
like a mentor to me.

00:04:37.616 --> 00:04:39.200
What makes this crime
even more horrendous

00:04:39.283 --> 00:04:42.366
is the victim was a
decorated officer of the law.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.908
Wait, you mean he was a cop?

00:04:44.991 --> 00:04:47.825
Please call your
first witness to the stand.

00:04:47.908 --> 00:04:50.408
Uh, my name is
Dick Gumshoe, your highness.

00:04:50.491 --> 00:04:52.616
I'm the head detective of
the homicide department

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.200
down at the precinct.

00:04:54.283 --> 00:04:56.658
[PHOENIX] This guy looks
like he's about to cry.

00:04:56.741 --> 00:04:57.991
Constable Byrde.

00:04:58.075 --> 00:05:00.408
Well. She's served me
and my squad faithfully

00:05:00.491 --> 00:05:01.491
and with respect!

00:05:01.575 --> 00:05:04.075
So you worked
under Detective Gumshoe?

00:05:04.158 --> 00:05:05.741
Sir! He's been a guiding force

00:05:05.825 --> 00:05:08.783
since I was a trainee.
A detective like no other.

00:05:08.866 --> 00:05:11.033
Detective. Can you tell us
about the murder?

00:05:11.116 --> 00:05:12.158
Sir!

00:05:15.075 --> 00:05:17.116
The crime took place
at "Exposé Park"

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.783
which is near the precinct.

00:05:18.866 --> 00:05:22.075
The victim was a local cop
named Dustin Prince.

00:05:22.158 --> 00:05:24.700
There were signs of blunt
force trauma on his body,

00:05:24.783 --> 00:05:26.658
and his neck was snapped.

00:05:26.741 --> 00:05:28.450
We believe he was
pushed over the railing

00:05:28.533 --> 00:05:30.950
from the path
several feet above.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:33.075
I'd like to add there
was a crucial piece of evidence

00:05:33.158 --> 00:05:35.033
found under the body.

00:05:35.116 --> 00:05:36.533
Here it is.

00:05:36.616 --> 00:05:38.116
It seems during the struggle,

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.783
the victim grabbed these
glasses off the killer's face,

00:05:40.866 --> 00:05:42.700
and held onto them as
he fell to the ground,

00:05:42.783 --> 00:05:44.575
breaking them and his neck.

00:05:44.658 --> 00:05:47.158
You think they're
the killer's glasses?

00:05:47.241 --> 00:05:48.408
What about those?

00:05:48.491 --> 00:05:50.908
Oh. Well, today
I'm wearing my spare pair.

00:05:50.991 --> 00:05:53.783
[PHOENIX] What? Then does that
mean the glasses are yours?

00:05:53.866 --> 00:05:55.950
No, the ones from
the scene aren't mine!

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:57.575
It just so happens that
I stepped on the ones

00:05:57.658 --> 00:05:59.783
I usually wear on that same day.

00:05:59.866 --> 00:06:01.450
Oh, yeah?

00:06:01.533 --> 00:06:04.491
It kinda goes with my
reputation of having bad luck.

00:06:04.575 --> 00:06:06.616
[JUDGE]
Defense, your cross-examination?

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.325
[PHOENIX] Me? You mean I have
to ask him questions, too?

00:06:09.408 --> 00:06:11.991
[JUDGE] That is the nature
of a cross-examination.

00:06:12.075 --> 00:06:14.741
Yes! Time for you
to flex your legal muscles!

00:06:14.825 --> 00:06:15.950
You've got this!

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:18.491
Question, what exactly
am I supposed to do?

00:06:18.575 --> 00:06:19.741
I'm lost.

00:06:19.825 --> 00:06:21.741
This is really not the
time to be making jokes!

00:06:21.825 --> 00:06:24.575
I know. I'm being
completely serious here.

00:06:24.658 --> 00:06:26.908
For some reason, I can't
remember anything right now.

00:06:26.991 --> 00:06:29.116
Huh? Wait!

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.575
Are you trying to tell me
that you have amnesia?

00:06:31.658 --> 00:06:33.241
I have amnesia?

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:35.158
And once again,
life proves that my nickname

00:06:35.241 --> 00:06:38.158
is devastatingly appropriate.

00:06:38.241 --> 00:06:40.825
Please begin your
cross-examination, defense.

00:06:40.908 --> 00:06:42.700
Look. Just go for it!

00:06:42.783 --> 00:06:46.241
Yeah, okay. So. The glasses.

00:06:47.283 --> 00:06:48.741
Do you have any
proof these do indeed

00:06:48.825 --> 00:06:50.241
belong to the defendant?

00:06:50.325 --> 00:06:52.491
The lenses are for
a person with near-sightedness

00:06:52.575 --> 00:06:55.408
and are almost the same
prescription as hers.

00:06:55.491 --> 00:06:57.491
And you can see,
the frames even kinda look like

00:06:57.575 --> 00:07:00.075
the ones she's
wearing in her ID.

00:07:00.158 --> 00:07:01.616
Wait a minute!

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:04.783
"Almost" and "kinda" are not
good enough in a murder case.

00:07:04.866 --> 00:07:06.033
[GUMSHOE groans]

00:07:07.241 --> 00:07:08.450
--[GUMSHOE squeals]
--Do you even have

00:07:08.533 --> 00:07:09.991
a shred of definitive proof?

00:07:10.075 --> 00:07:11.116
One moment!

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.658
If definitive proof
is what you need,

00:07:12.741 --> 00:07:15.533
look no further
than this photograph!

00:07:15.616 --> 00:07:16.866
[CROWD gasping]

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.700
[PHOENIX]
Uh. That says Maggie?

00:07:18.783 --> 00:07:20.033
[JUDGE]
Indeed it does.

00:07:20.116 --> 00:07:22.741
Which as we know,
is the name of the defendant.

00:07:22.825 --> 00:07:25.616
[MAGGEY] It's all a setup!
A big fraud! Fake!

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:27.450
[JUDGE]
Order! Order!

00:07:29.616 --> 00:07:32.200
[PHOENIX] If the victim wrote
her name as a dying message.

00:07:32.283 --> 00:07:33.658
We are completely hosed.

00:07:33.741 --> 00:07:34.825
[MAGGEY sighs]

00:07:34.908 --> 00:07:35.866
[PHOENIX grunts]

00:07:37.908 --> 00:07:39.200
[PHOENIX]
Wait.

00:07:39.283 --> 00:07:40.991
--Hold it!
--[yells]

00:07:41.075 --> 00:07:42.825
Oof. That always
hits me like a punch

00:07:42.908 --> 00:07:45.533
to the breadbasket.
My poor belly.

00:07:45.616 --> 00:07:46.866
[PHOENIX]
What was that all about?

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:48.283
It was just an instinct.

00:07:48.366 --> 00:07:50.616
Like I had to yell out as
loud as I could and point

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.491
my finger at him.

00:07:52.575 --> 00:07:54.241
Detective, I'd like you
to clearly state

00:07:54.325 --> 00:07:55.741
the defendant's name for us.

00:07:55.825 --> 00:07:57.950
Uh. Well, it's
Maggey Byrde, of course.

00:07:58.033 --> 00:07:59.575
And would you mind
telling the court exactly

00:07:59.658 --> 00:08:01.075
how she spells her name?

00:08:01.158 --> 00:08:02.825
[PAYNE] Hold it! The question
is pointless, your honor.

00:08:02.908 --> 00:08:04.658
It's right there in the photo!

00:08:04.741 --> 00:08:07.200
It's true that this message
does spell "Maggie."

00:08:07.283 --> 00:08:11.283
But. Her name is
spelled M-a-g-g-e-y.

00:08:11.366 --> 00:08:14.241
[gasping]

00:08:14.325 --> 00:08:17.366
The contradiction
of facts is undeniable!

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.700
[PAYNE] But have you considered
the possibility that the victim

00:08:19.783 --> 00:08:22.075
didn't know about
her peculiar spelling?

00:08:23.158 --> 00:08:25.450
Surely, you recall
what you said earlier.

00:08:25.533 --> 00:08:29.283
Constable Byrd stands accused
of brutally murdering her lover!

00:08:29.366 --> 00:08:32.033
There's no way he wouldn't
know something like that!

00:08:32.116 --> 00:08:33.533
[yells]

00:08:33.616 --> 00:08:35.783
Tragically, the day
Officer Prince was murdered

00:08:35.866 --> 00:08:37.700
also happened to be
his birthday, and Maggey

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:40.366
had gotten him a present
to celebrate the occasion.

00:08:41.241 --> 00:08:43.491
[PHOENIX]
I guess this is it?

00:08:43.575 --> 00:08:45.908
That is an extremely
yellow glove.

00:08:45.991 --> 00:08:47.491
Yeah, it is!

00:08:47.575 --> 00:08:49.908
He was a huge baseball fan and
yellow was his favorite color!

00:08:49.991 --> 00:08:52.033
Oh. And does that
yellow glove have

00:08:52.116 --> 00:08:54.575
any kind of relevance to
this case whatsoever?

00:08:54.658 --> 00:08:56.908
Uh. Well. Not sure.

00:08:56.991 --> 00:09:00.033
[CROWD murmuring]

00:09:00.116 --> 00:09:02.408
Yes! In fact, that
blindingly yellow glove

00:09:02.491 --> 00:09:04.658
holds the key to
this entire case!

00:09:04.741 --> 00:09:06.033
[gasping]

00:09:06.116 --> 00:09:07.450
If you look closely.

00:09:07.533 --> 00:09:09.700
You can see that it's made
for a left-handed player!

00:09:09.783 --> 00:09:11.283
Ah...

00:09:11.366 --> 00:09:13.366
[PHOENIX] Hmph. And now,
let's take another look

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:14.783
at the crime scene photo.

00:09:14.866 --> 00:09:16.908
--[gasping]
--That's the wrong hand!

00:09:16.991 --> 00:09:18.241
Good catch!

00:09:18.325 --> 00:09:20.366
Dustin did always like to
call himself a southpaw!

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.366
There's no way a lefty
would use his other hand

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:26.408
to write his final message.
So the only explanation is...

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.533
...the victim was not
the one who wrote it!

00:09:32.616 --> 00:09:33.866
[yells]

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:36.116
[CROWD gasping, murmuring]

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:37.533
[PHOENIX]
What happened?

00:09:37.616 --> 00:09:41.158
It's like before. This sudden
rush just takes over.

00:09:41.241 --> 00:09:43.783
A jolt of energy
surges through my body!

00:09:44.741 --> 00:09:47.033
If the prosecution has
nothing further to add--

00:09:47.116 --> 00:09:48.908
[PAYNE]
Hold it! Uh, Your Honor,

00:09:48.991 --> 00:09:52.075
the prosecution is not ready
to rest its case at this moment!

00:09:52.158 --> 00:09:53.366
--[gasping]
--You have more?

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:54.366
Oh, no!

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:55.783
Yes, I do.

00:09:55.866 --> 00:09:58.325
It so happens there was an
eyewitness to the murder.

00:09:58.408 --> 00:09:59.575
[CROWD murmuring]

00:09:59.658 --> 00:10:00.783
[PAYNE] They were at the
scene the very moment

00:10:00.866 --> 00:10:03.200
poor Officer Prince was
pushed to his death!

00:10:03.283 --> 00:10:05.366
In fact, they were close
enough to clearly see

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:06.991
the face of the assailant!

00:10:07.075 --> 00:10:10.533
But I'm telling you.
It was not me!

00:10:10.616 --> 00:10:13.116
[JUDGE] Bring this witness
to the stand at once!

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.908
[PAYNE] Sir, meet the drifter
who was trying to take

00:10:14.991 --> 00:10:17.158
a nice walk in the park
when he was subjected

00:10:17.241 --> 00:10:18.783
to this horrible crime!

00:10:18.866 --> 00:10:19.825
Hi!

00:10:23.033 --> 00:10:23.991
[MAGGEY, PHOENIX grunt]

00:10:32.283 --> 00:10:33.908
[PHOENIX]
He saw the murder?

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:38.491
[PAYNE] Will you please state
your name for the record?

00:10:38.575 --> 00:10:40.866
[WELLINGTON] Yes, but first, I'd
like to make a clarification.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.283
You just introduced my fabulous
personage to the court

00:10:43.366 --> 00:10:45.283
as "a drifter taking a walk"!

00:10:45.366 --> 00:10:47.283
Oh, well, I suppose I did.

00:10:47.366 --> 00:10:49.325
I simply cannot abide
such a biased assessment

00:10:49.408 --> 00:10:50.825
of my character.
[speaking speed increases]

00:10:50.908 --> 00:10:51.991
True, calling me a university
student would be a bit of

00:10:52.075 --> 00:10:53.241
a stretch at this precise
moment in time.

00:10:53.325 --> 00:10:54.700
But as a man who will
settle for nothing less

00:10:54.783 --> 00:10:55.866
than the absolute finest of
everything that this world

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.200
has to offer, I find
myself searching for

00:10:57.283 --> 00:10:58.325
the learning institution
worthy of my intellect...

00:10:58.408 --> 00:11:00.116
Yes! I hope you'll
pardon my confusion!

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:02.158
Only top tier fashion,
cars, women,

00:11:02.241 --> 00:11:04.408
and glasses for moi,
And that's why.

00:11:04.491 --> 00:11:06.366
I can't choose a university.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:08.283
[PHOENIX]
Why did he mention glasses?

00:11:10.325 --> 00:11:12.866
I believe Mr. Payne
only asked for your name.

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:15.991
Well, I'm sorry.
But he should already know that.

00:11:16.075 --> 00:11:17.450
If I must state the obvious,

00:11:17.533 --> 00:11:19.741
I am Richard Wellington,
and I am, in essence,

00:11:19.825 --> 00:11:21.033
a university student.

00:11:21.116 --> 00:11:22.991
[PHOENIX] What does he
mean by "in essence"?

00:11:23.075 --> 00:11:25.575
If I may, I'd like to
begin my testimony.

00:11:27.783 --> 00:11:29.283
I was strolling
through Exposé Park

00:11:29.366 --> 00:11:32.283
that evening, when suddenly,
before my very eyes!

00:11:32.366 --> 00:11:34.950
It was as if the
officer had fallen from the sky.

00:11:35.033 --> 00:11:37.325
In a panic, I looked up and
locked my gaze with a woman

00:11:37.408 --> 00:11:39.533
who looked positively aghast!

00:11:39.616 --> 00:11:41.866
It's her. I'm sure of it!

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:43.908
--[MAGGEY growls]
--[CROWD whispering]

00:11:43.991 --> 00:11:46.408
[PHOENIX] Was there anything
else that caught your attention?

00:11:46.491 --> 00:11:48.700
[WELLINGTON]
Hmm. Let me think.

00:11:48.783 --> 00:11:51.825
Oddly enough a bunch
of bananas fell with him!

00:11:51.908 --> 00:11:54.241
Uh. Bananas? That's very odd.

00:11:54.325 --> 00:11:55.825
True. But there they were...

00:11:55.908 --> 00:11:57.825
...remarkably yellow
and quite appealing.

00:11:57.908 --> 00:12:00.825
[PHOENIX
"Remarkably yellow bananas"?

00:12:00.908 --> 00:12:02.950
[PHOENIX] Can you describe
them in more detail?

00:12:03.033 --> 00:12:05.533
Why? They're lying
right there in front of you.

00:12:05.616 --> 00:12:06.700
[gasping]

00:12:06.783 --> 00:12:08.575
Is that so?

00:12:08.658 --> 00:12:10.950
You said they looked appetizing,
so would you like to

00:12:11.033 --> 00:12:12.158
try a bite of one?

00:12:12.241 --> 00:12:13.616
[WELLINGTON]
Hmm...

00:12:14.866 --> 00:12:18.825
[screams]
It can't be. That's bananas!

00:12:18.908 --> 00:12:21.075
And how good is
your eyesight, by the way?

00:12:21.158 --> 00:12:23.325
Hey, what does my vision
have to do with this?

00:12:23.408 --> 00:12:24.658
Objection!

00:12:24.741 --> 00:12:26.408
That baseball glove could
easily be mistaken for

00:12:26.491 --> 00:12:27.783
a bunch of bananas!

00:12:27.866 --> 00:12:29.741
I'll allow the
line of questioning.

00:12:29.825 --> 00:12:32.700
Both eyes are
twenty-two hundred. Okay?

00:12:32.783 --> 00:12:36.366
"Twenty-two hundred"?
That's definitely not very good.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.575
Is there a reason
you're not wearing

00:12:37.658 --> 00:12:39.158
your glasses today?

00:12:39.241 --> 00:12:42.491
[WELLINGTON gulps] Of course.
Because I recently lost them.

00:12:42.575 --> 00:12:45.575
Lost them? Maybe I can help.

00:12:45.658 --> 00:12:47.158
Might these belong to you?

00:12:47.241 --> 00:12:51.075
[gasps]
Wait. Where did you find them?

00:12:51.158 --> 00:12:52.741
The police found them
crushed beneath

00:12:52.825 --> 00:12:54.075
Officer Prince's body.

00:12:54.158 --> 00:12:56.450
Oh, my god! That can't be true!

00:12:56.533 --> 00:12:57.658
[PHOENIX]
Mr. Wellington.

00:12:57.741 --> 00:12:59.825
Can you explain why they
would turn up there?

00:12:59.908 --> 00:13:01.491
[CROWD gasping]

00:13:01.575 --> 00:13:03.033
How would I know?!

00:13:03.116 --> 00:13:04.908
And besides the victim clearly
told us in the sand message

00:13:04.991 --> 00:13:07.491
that it was Maggie who
murdered him, not me.

00:13:07.575 --> 00:13:09.241
Sure, he did
write down "Maggie,"

00:13:09.325 --> 00:13:11.200
but her name is
spelled this way.

00:13:11.283 --> 00:13:12.616
--[gasps]
--No!

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:14.658
[PHOENIX] The real killer made
a conspicuous mistake by

00:13:14.741 --> 00:13:16.783
using the victim's right hand.

00:13:16.866 --> 00:13:18.283
Since the victim
was left-handed,

00:13:18.366 --> 00:13:21.325
this was just a ham-fisted
attempt to frame Ms. Byrde.

00:13:21.408 --> 00:13:22.658
That may be the case,

00:13:22.741 --> 00:13:24.616
but obviously the murderer
would still have to know

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.200
her first name to try to
frame her in such a way.

00:13:27.283 --> 00:13:29.575
It couldn't have been me,
because I don't know her at all.

00:13:29.658 --> 00:13:31.158
--[laughs]
--[MAGGEY growls]

00:13:31.241 --> 00:13:33.783
[PHOENIX] Ms. Byrde. You don't
know him either, do you?

00:13:33.866 --> 00:13:36.908
No, sir. But since you
brought up my name...

00:13:36.991 --> 00:13:39.283
That day, when Dustin and I were
walking around the park,

00:13:39.366 --> 00:13:42.033
we happened to find
a cell phone.

00:13:42.116 --> 00:13:43.950
This is Maggey, are you
trying to get ahold of

00:13:44.033 --> 00:13:45.283
the owner of this phone?

00:13:45.366 --> 00:13:47.241
[WELLINGTON] Great!
This is my phone, actually!

00:13:47.325 --> 00:13:48.491
I lost it!

00:13:48.575 --> 00:13:51.908
You're in luck! I just
found it at Exposé Park!

00:13:51.991 --> 00:13:53.491
[WELLINGTON]
I'll be there shortly!

00:13:55.408 --> 00:13:57.450
So. Dustin and I
waited at the park

00:13:57.533 --> 00:14:01.866
for what seemed like forever.
He needed to head back home.

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:05.450
Right after he left,
I heard him scream.

00:14:05.533 --> 00:14:07.200
And then I saw him.

00:14:07.283 --> 00:14:08.366
[PHOENIX]
Hmm.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:12.075
[PHOENIX]
Maggey's name. It all adds up!

00:14:12.158 --> 00:14:15.825
[PHOENIX] Tell me. Did you also
lose your cell phone recently?

00:14:15.908 --> 00:14:17.450
What? Why would that matter?

00:14:17.533 --> 00:14:19.491
[PHOENIX] I can assume that you
tried calling your own number

00:14:19.575 --> 00:14:20.491
to locate it.

00:14:20.575 --> 00:14:21.950
And what does that prove?

00:14:22.033 --> 00:14:24.116
[PHOENIX] For one,
that you found out her name.

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:26.033
She answered with
"this is Maggey," right?

00:14:26.116 --> 00:14:27.616
[WELLINGTON growls]

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.700
[PHOENIX] Just hearing the name,
one would think it would look.

00:14:29.783 --> 00:14:31.908
Exactly like this.

00:14:31.991 --> 00:14:33.450
Since you heard it,
you weren't aware of

00:14:33.533 --> 00:14:35.033
its unusual spelling.

00:14:35.116 --> 00:14:36.408
[gasps]

00:14:36.491 --> 00:14:38.450
You might as well admit it.

00:14:38.533 --> 00:14:41.325
You killed officer
Dustin Prince.

00:14:41.408 --> 00:14:42.783
Isn't that right?

00:14:42.866 --> 00:14:44.200
[screams]

00:14:44.283 --> 00:14:45.366
Objection!

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.575
The witness has
no motive for the murder!

00:14:47.658 --> 00:14:49.200
[gasping]

00:14:49.283 --> 00:14:50.533
Y-Yes, that's true!

00:14:50.616 --> 00:14:53.075
Why would a scholar like me
want to kill a cop?

00:14:53.158 --> 00:14:54.658
Indeed.

00:14:54.741 --> 00:14:56.783
Well, defense, do you care to
explain what motive the witness

00:14:56.866 --> 00:14:59.325
could have had to
commit such a crime?

00:14:59.408 --> 00:15:00.575
Your Honor...

00:15:00.658 --> 00:15:01.700
[chuckles]

00:15:01.783 --> 00:15:03.158
They had never met.

00:15:03.241 --> 00:15:07.283
So, what could the reason
to kill Prince possibly be?

00:15:07.366 --> 00:15:09.325
[PHOENIX] There's something
right on the tip of my tongue.

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:12.533
Something about the case,
but I can't remember what it is!

00:15:12.616 --> 00:15:16.241
Ahem. If the defense is unable
to provide a motive, then--

00:15:16.325 --> 00:15:17.450
[MAYA]
Hold it!

00:15:20.783 --> 00:15:22.700
[MAYA] I'm sorry
I kept you waiting, Nick!

00:15:22.783 --> 00:15:23.783
[gasps]

00:15:23.866 --> 00:15:26.075
[MAYA]
I was so afraid I was too late.

00:15:26.158 --> 00:15:29.491
Just in the nick of time!
Way to go, Maya!

00:15:29.575 --> 00:15:30.700
Hey there, Maya.

00:15:30.783 --> 00:15:32.283
[MAYA]
Don't you worry.

00:15:32.366 --> 00:15:34.450
I've come to save the day, with
this super-important evidence!

00:15:34.533 --> 00:15:36.200
[PHOENIX]
Hm?

00:15:36.283 --> 00:15:38.783
Feast your eyes on this!

00:15:38.866 --> 00:15:39.991
What is it?

00:15:40.075 --> 00:15:41.366
It's this crazy list
you had me put together

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:42.450
just for you!

00:15:42.533 --> 00:15:43.700
O... kay.

00:15:43.783 --> 00:15:46.158
It wasn't easy compiling
all that stuff, ya know?

00:15:46.241 --> 00:15:49.408
[PHOENIX sighs] A bunch of
names and phone numbers.

00:15:49.491 --> 00:15:51.408
Uh, thanks. But what
does it all mean?

00:15:51.491 --> 00:15:52.700
Huh?

00:15:52.783 --> 00:15:54.408
You mean you don't
remember asking me to gather

00:15:54.491 --> 00:15:55.825
all that info?!

00:15:55.908 --> 00:15:57.575
The names and numbers
are all of the contacts I found

00:15:57.658 --> 00:15:59.450
in the phone
I picked up that day!

00:15:59.533 --> 00:16:00.991
And the crazy thing is,

00:16:01.075 --> 00:16:03.325
every last one of them belongs
to a ring of local con men!

00:16:03.408 --> 00:16:04.575
[WELLINGTON gasps]

00:16:04.658 --> 00:16:08.658
[PHOENIX] A ring of con
men. Cell phone. Names.

00:16:09.991 --> 00:16:12.908
Defense. Please wrap
up your cross-examination.

00:16:12.991 --> 00:16:15.908
[PHOENIX] I get it. This is
what I was trying to remember!

00:16:15.991 --> 00:16:17.908
Do you know where
that cell phone is now?

00:16:17.991 --> 00:16:20.158
I'm pretty sure you
have it, don't you?

00:16:20.241 --> 00:16:21.408
[gasps]

00:16:21.491 --> 00:16:22.700
Yeah, I gave it to you
right when I hired you

00:16:22.783 --> 00:16:24.241
to defend me.

00:16:24.325 --> 00:16:25.408
Huh.

00:16:26.575 --> 00:16:27.866
See? I knew you had it.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:28.908
Yep!

00:16:28.991 --> 00:16:30.241
Thank you, miss.

00:16:30.325 --> 00:16:32.283
You handed me the
last piece of the puzzle.

00:16:32.366 --> 00:16:33.825
"Miss"?

00:16:33.908 --> 00:16:36.283
[PHOENIX] Your Honor,
I have the motive right here!

00:16:36.366 --> 00:16:37.741
--[CROWD gasping]
--[JUDGE] What is it?

00:16:37.825 --> 00:16:38.991
[WELLINGTON gasps]

00:16:39.075 --> 00:16:40.700
The cell phone the
defendant found that day.

00:16:40.783 --> 00:16:43.200
When we investigated the
list of contacts stored on it,

00:16:43.283 --> 00:16:46.200
we discovered that they were all
part of a ring of con artists.

00:16:46.283 --> 00:16:48.200
[PAYNE]
Say what?!

00:16:48.283 --> 00:16:50.700
Tell me. The names
and numbers on this device

00:16:50.783 --> 00:16:52.741
all belong to your
associates, do they not?

00:16:52.825 --> 00:16:54.241
Objection!

00:16:54.325 --> 00:16:55.908
If the witness was told that
it would be returned to him

00:16:55.991 --> 00:16:57.908
without incident,
then why on earth would he

00:16:57.991 --> 00:16:59.616
have to kill to get it back?

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.866
Because of who
he saw waiting for him.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:03.825
And what they were wearing.

00:17:03.908 --> 00:17:04.825
[MAGGEY gasps]

00:17:04.908 --> 00:17:06.783
[MAYA]
A policeman's uniform!

00:17:06.866 --> 00:17:09.033
Yes. Constable Prince
was still wearing

00:17:09.116 --> 00:17:11.991
his uniform when he met
with Ms. Byrde that day.

00:17:12.075 --> 00:17:13.616
Which led you to make
the assumption that she had

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:17.658
brought a cop along to arrest
you, right, Mr. Wellington?

00:17:17.741 --> 00:17:18.866
You were worried that
they had checked out

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:20.616
some of the contacts
in your phone.

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:23.575
And that they knew you were
one of those con men, too.

00:17:23.658 --> 00:17:26.575
So you went into a panic
and pushed Officer Prince

00:17:26.658 --> 00:17:29.116
over the railing to his death!

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:32.450
[WELLINGTON giggles, laughs]

00:17:34.366 --> 00:17:36.783
Oh, my. Not bad for
a third-rate lawyer!

00:17:36.866 --> 00:17:38.450
And what's so funny?

00:17:38.533 --> 00:17:39.616
[WELLINGTON]
The joke's on you.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.200
That's not my cell phone!

00:17:41.283 --> 00:17:42.200
[gasps]

00:17:42.283 --> 00:17:43.491
[WELLINGTON chuckles]

00:17:46.033 --> 00:17:47.033
[gasps]

00:17:47.116 --> 00:17:48.908
They really have
the exact same model?

00:17:48.991 --> 00:17:50.575
It's true I had
misplaced my phone,

00:17:50.658 --> 00:17:52.658
but I found it shortly after.

00:17:52.741 --> 00:17:54.200
Yeah, but unfortunately,

00:17:54.283 --> 00:17:57.658
all my contacts went "poof"--
vanished into the ether.

00:17:57.741 --> 00:17:59.866
It must've glitched
when I dropped it.

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:02.491
[PHOENIX] He erased those
numbers to hide the evidence.

00:18:02.575 --> 00:18:04.700
"A ring of local con artists"?

00:18:04.783 --> 00:18:06.783
What a pathetic
defense that was.

00:18:06.866 --> 00:18:08.533
Nick. What are we gonna do?

00:18:08.616 --> 00:18:10.616
Lucky for you, you
found your phone.

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:12.200
Will you tell us where it was?

00:18:12.283 --> 00:18:13.825
Will I?

00:18:13.908 --> 00:18:18.283
[chuckles]
You've got to be kidding me.

00:18:18.366 --> 00:18:21.825
The only thing you need
to know is that this is it!

00:18:21.908 --> 00:18:24.116
Enough! Control yourself!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.450
[grunts]
Ow.

00:18:28.533 --> 00:18:31.533
[cell jingle plays]

00:18:31.616 --> 00:18:33.283
[PHOENIX gasps]
Guess they hung up.

00:18:33.366 --> 00:18:35.741
[blow lands]

00:18:35.825 --> 00:18:37.825
[PHOENIX]
It's all coming back to me now.

00:18:37.908 --> 00:18:41.158
The moment when it happened.
I heard that ringtone.

00:18:41.241 --> 00:18:43.533
If you were hoping to find
any evidence on this thing,

00:18:43.616 --> 00:18:46.491
it's gone with your
chance for victory!

00:18:46.575 --> 00:18:47.700
[cackles]

00:18:47.783 --> 00:18:51.325
I really thought we had
him with that list.

00:18:51.408 --> 00:18:53.366
But I guess he turned
the tables on us.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:54.408
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:18:54.491 --> 00:18:56.366
[PHOENIX]
"Turned the tables"?

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:59.200
Then all I gotta do is
turn them back on him!

00:18:59.283 --> 00:19:00.200
[MAYA]
Here you go.

00:19:00.283 --> 00:19:03.616
Aww. Thank you, young lady.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.783
The defense appears
to be out of questions,

00:19:05.866 --> 00:19:07.908
so that concludes the
cross-examination.

00:19:07.991 --> 00:19:11.116
Well, my work here is done, so
time to say toodle-oo!

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:12.575
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:19:17.575 --> 00:19:19.408
Ah! What is he doing to me?

00:19:19.491 --> 00:19:20.491
[gasping]

00:19:20.575 --> 00:19:21.783
Sorry to burst your bubble,

00:19:21.866 --> 00:19:23.950
but I have more
evidence against you.

00:19:24.033 --> 00:19:25.741
Wanna hear what it is?

00:19:25.825 --> 00:19:27.116
What nonsense!

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:29.325
[PHOENIX] Maya, will you
do me a favor, please?

00:19:29.408 --> 00:19:30.491
Call my cell phone.

00:19:30.575 --> 00:19:32.908
So. You want me
to call you right now?

00:19:32.991 --> 00:19:34.241
Okie-doke.

00:19:34.325 --> 00:19:36.283
[PHOENIX] This will prove
my point. You'll see.

00:19:36.366 --> 00:19:37.866
[MAYA]
All right, I'm calling you.

00:19:38.575 --> 00:19:40.491
[different cell jingle plays]

00:19:40.575 --> 00:19:41.700
[PHOENIX]
What?

00:19:41.783 --> 00:19:43.366
You did call my phone
number, didn't you?

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.533
[MAYA]
Mm-hmm. Hold on.

00:19:46.616 --> 00:19:48.575
Wait. Why would
my phone be ringing?

00:19:48.658 --> 00:19:50.741
It's quite simple, because
the phone you're holding

00:19:50.825 --> 00:19:52.450
now actually belongs to me.

00:19:52.533 --> 00:19:54.283
No way!

00:19:54.366 --> 00:19:55.783
In case you're wondering,

00:19:55.866 --> 00:19:57.866
that lump on the head you gave
me is starting to go down.

00:19:57.950 --> 00:19:59.200
[WELLINGTON growls]

00:19:59.283 --> 00:20:01.325
It's pretty easy to figure
out how it all happened.

00:20:01.408 --> 00:20:03.825
You knocked me unconscious and
tried to take your cell back.

00:20:03.908 --> 00:20:06.241
But. You picked up
mine by mistake.

00:20:06.325 --> 00:20:08.200
[whimpers]

00:20:08.283 --> 00:20:11.116
The truth is calling and you're
accepting the charges!

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:14.450
[screams]

00:20:14.533 --> 00:20:16.241
[JUDGE]
Now that we've re-convened,

00:20:16.325 --> 00:20:17.658
where is your witness?

00:20:17.741 --> 00:20:20.241
Well. He was arrested
during the recess, Your Honor.

00:20:20.325 --> 00:20:21.950
It's been a while since
I've seen you put on

00:20:22.033 --> 00:20:23.616
such a show, Mr. Wright.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:26.033
[gasps]
Oh, yeah.

00:20:26.116 --> 00:20:28.783
I hereby conclude the
trial of Ms. Maggey Byrde

00:20:28.866 --> 00:20:31.491
and I am prepared
to hand down my verdict.

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:34.741
Not guilty!

00:20:34.825 --> 00:20:36.950
[CROWD cheers, applauds]

00:20:37.033 --> 00:20:38.741
Thank you, Your Honor!

00:20:38.825 --> 00:20:41.366
[JUDGE] That is all!
This court is adjourned!

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:44.658
[MAYA]
You had amnesia?

00:20:44.741 --> 00:20:47.158
I guess you were acting
pretty weird earlier.

00:20:47.241 --> 00:20:49.408
And you don't usually
call me "miss" like that.

00:20:49.491 --> 00:20:50.991
Well, I'm feeling better now.

00:20:51.075 --> 00:20:52.700
I truly appreciate
everything you've done

00:20:52.783 --> 00:20:56.825
for me today. Now that it's
over, I think I'm gonna cry!

00:20:56.908 --> 00:21:00.366
[GUMSHOE] Maggey!
Congratulations on the verdict!

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:02.325
Thanks for all the
support in there, Dick!

00:21:02.408 --> 00:21:04.283
[GUMSHOE groans] That's fair,
but I never thought

00:21:04.366 --> 00:21:05.908
you could have actually done it.

00:21:05.991 --> 00:21:07.616
I'm gonna take this
opportunity and turn it

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:09.783
into a new lease on life!

00:21:09.866 --> 00:21:11.950
And I'll bet
the next time we meet.

00:21:12.033 --> 00:21:14.533
I'm gonna have more good luck
than I'll know what to do with!

00:21:14.616 --> 00:21:15.783
Now that's the spirit!

00:21:15.866 --> 00:21:17.283
We're gonna have
to start calling you,

00:21:17.366 --> 00:21:20.450
the "goddess of good-fortune!"
Right? Don't you think so?

00:21:20.533 --> 00:21:23.491
Yep. Totally! Wait a sec.

00:21:23.575 --> 00:21:25.116
What's up?

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:28.033
We've met before,
haven't we, miss?

00:21:28.116 --> 00:21:29.533
Oh, no way!

00:21:29.616 --> 00:21:31.908
Nick, please don't tell me
you still have amnesia!

00:21:31.991 --> 00:21:33.700
I'm just kidding with you, Maya!

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:38.116
[PHOENIX]
My name is Phoenix Wright,

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.950
and I'm a defense attorney.

00:21:40.033 --> 00:21:42.491
No matter how high
the odds are stacked against us.

00:21:42.575 --> 00:21:44.866
It's my job to stand up for
those who have no one else

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:46.200
in their corner.

00:21:46.283 --> 00:21:48.741
I'll do whatever it takes
to fight for the truth!

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:22.158
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:22.241 --> 00:23:24.450
The phantom thief,
Mask DeMasque,

00:23:24.533 --> 00:23:27.116
has stolen the sacred urn
from Kurain Village.

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:28.825
Maya's childhood home.

00:23:28.908 --> 00:23:30.033
And to make things worse,

00:23:30.116 --> 00:23:32.408
the stolen urn
goes missing again!

00:23:32.491 --> 00:23:34.908
As the plot continues
to thicken, a bizarre detective

00:23:34.991 --> 00:23:36.200
and the shady
characters surrounding

00:23:36.283 --> 00:23:38.158
the phantom thief
enter the fray.

00:23:38.241 --> 00:23:39.950
What's more, the
prosecutor waiting for us

00:23:40.033 --> 00:23:42.200
in the courtroom is
yet another mystery!

00:23:42.283 --> 00:23:44.783
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:44.866 --> 00:23:47.825
Next episode: "The
Stolen Turnabout - First Trial"!

00:23:47.908 --> 00:23:49.033
Take that!
